    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event for owner creation, keeping the existing audit line intact.\n\n**New files** (in `.../rest/function/owner/`):\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 an immutable `record(long seq, int ownerId, String customerCode, int membershipLevel)` with `EVENT = \"OWNER_CREATED\"`. Its `toJson()` serializes to the exact canonical object `{\"seq\":..,\"ownerId\":..,\"customerCode\":..,\"membershipLevel\":..,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, with proper JSON string escaping. One responsibility: model and serialize the event.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEventSequence.java`** \u2014 a `@Component` singleton wrapping an `AtomicLong`, whose `next()` yields the monotonically increasing `seq` **across all creates** (a single app-wide sequence, not per-request). Injected into the function by type, exactly like the existing `IdempotencyStore`.\n\n**Edits:**\n- **`Owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()`** \u2014 a new derived getter returning `customerCode` today. This is the single source of truth for \"which field is the owner's primary identifier\"; when the customer code is later unified into a member id, only this method changes and the event follows automatically. It maps through `OwnerMapper`\u2192`OwnerDto`, which has no such property, so it doesn't leak into responses.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 after emitting the existing human-readable audit line, it now also emits the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` (built from `owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()` and `sequence.next()`) as JSON via the same `AUDIT` logger. Using the single-argument `AUDIT.info(String)` overload means the JSON braces aren't treated as SLF4J placeholders.\n\nThe design keeps each concern in its own small unit: sequencing in the sequence bean, serialization in the event record, \"what identifies an owner\" on the entity, and orchestration in the audit function \u2014 nothing became a catch-all.\n\nObserved output confirms both lines:\n```\nINFO AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=... membershipLevel=1 membershipNumber=...\nINFO AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nFull suite: **16 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
